WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.802
In Microsoft Fabric, be careful about which SQL surface you are using.

00:00:03.802 --> 00:00:07.142
A Spark notebook or Spark SQL cell runs through Spark.

00:00:07.142 --> 00:00:13.232
A SQL analytics endpoint uses a different SQL serving surface, often with T-SQL style behavior.

00:00:13.232 --> 00:00:15.592
Some syntax and capabilities differ.

00:00:15.592 --> 00:00:19.112
When code fails, first check which engine you are actually using.

00:00:19.112 --> 00:00:23.087
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:23.087 --> 00:00:28.387
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:28.387 --> 00:00:30.432
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:30.432 --> 00:00:35.802
In a real setting such as a retail pipeline aggregating high-volume sales data across partitions,

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:41.342
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:41.342 --> 00:00:42.762
before discussing syntax.

00:00:42.762 --> 00:00:48.320
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
